{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells","id":1534903,"title":"Wards and trigger spells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-29T09:19:03-07:00","id":1534903,"title":"Wards and trigger spells","content":"I cant wrap my head how exactly do wards work. Anyone could explain this? For example a ward made to burn vampires who enter the area.<br /> <br /> As for trigger spells. When does the mage roll? At cast or at trigger time? If the latter does the mage know how well he cast the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T09:48:37-07:00","id":1534907,"title":"","content":"Those have always been so confusing to me that I just use my house rules and I barely remember the official ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T09:56:47-07:00","id":1534908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534907#post1534907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those have always been so confusing to me that I just use my house rules and I barely remember the official ones</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T12:24:29-07:00","id":1534916,"title":"","content":"I can give you my approach. Fair warning, this is what I came up with as I was beating my head against the wall over the terrible ward writeups. It hasn't come up in my games and so I haven't playtested it.<br /> <br /> <b>Trigger Conditions</b> - Wards and Trigger spells are confusing because the depend on something that is never given rules: sometimes spells need to be able to sense or determine or in some other way restrict themselves to their intended targets. Trigger spells need to be able to determine when the trigger conditions happen. Your ward needs to be set for Vampires.<br /> <br /> My method is this always takes the relevant spheres at rank 2. Setting triggers does not involve transmuting, altering, or in any way affecting a pattern so the rank doesn't vary with the target. Instead it functions like sensory magic. Rank 1 is sufficient to detect anything appropriate to the sphere. Rank 2 is sufficient to add that to a spell. Setting triggers against iron is Matter 2, against cats is Life 2, and against Vampires is Life 2/Matter 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Wards</b> - By default Correspondence 2 can set wards that inhibit or enhance the actions of targets within the ward (difficulty modifiers) and Ward 4 can actually bar entry or exit. Anything else requires adding that capacity. Because this does affect the relevant patterns it requires the Spheres at the appropriate level to cast the effect being added to the ward. SEP fields (Somebody Else's Problem) require Mind 2, for instance, and fire attacks require Forces 2 and an appropriate source of fire.<br /> <br /> Unlike teleports this does not require higher levels of Correspondence for higher associated spheres.<br /> <br /> So your vampire ward is Corr 2 (for the ward), Life 2/Matter 2 (to set it for Vampires), and Forces 2 or Forces 3/Prime 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T01:27:49-07:00","id":1534933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534916#post1534916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Trigger Conditions</b> - Wards and Trigger spells are confusing because the depend on something that is never given rules: sometimes spells need to be able to sense or determine or in some other way restrict themselves to their intended targets. Trigger spells need to be able to determine when the trigger conditions happen. Your ward needs to be set for Vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could be future scrying. So you transport the spell in time till something happens.<br /> When do you roll for arete? when you create the trigger or when it triggers?<br /> <br /> Are wards vulgar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T06:57:24-07:00","id":1534942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534933#post1534933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be future scrying. So you transport the spell in time till something happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, in which case the trigger needs to be set for Vampires, and I use the same Rank 2 guideline for that. Indeed I use that guideline for situations where a spell has a special interaction with the domain of a sphere but doesn't alter the domain or use any of the powers of that sphere. Locking is another case of this, and M20 is pretty consistent on using (Pattern Sphere) 2 for locking.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me. Since wards need to last for a while it is a good idea to lock them to avoid concentration issues. Time trigger spells already bypass concentration issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When do you roll for arete? when you create the trigger or when it triggers? </div> </div> </div>You roll arete when the spell is cast. So you roll at the creation of the ward or the time trigger, not when they activate. The idea with both of those spells is that they exist whether they are actively doing something or not. The mage doesn't need to carry around the components for them use his casting action for the turn to fire them off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are wards vulgar? </div> </div> </div>Vulgarity, as it pertains to casting difficulty and paradox accrual, is determined by what the consensus thinks of the spell when it is cast. Because Wards don't tend to have visible effects at casting, they are usually coincidental. Reality might object when they start getting active, but that objection will manifest as unbelief rather than paradox points or backlashes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T07:29:11-07:00","id":1534945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534933#post1534933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When do you roll for arete? when you create the trigger or when it triggers?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you create the Trigger. This isn't specified in any general rule AFAIK, but the Trigger it's part of the Effect itself and not a sepparate Effect - remember that you can't cast more than one Effect per Arete roll, but you <i>can </i>cast an Effect that does several things at once (you can see how this works in, say, the <a href=\"https://denvermage.fandom.com/wiki/Rotes_-_Traditions#Iron_Avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Iron Avatar</a> of the Euthanatos)<br /> <br /> One of the main uses of Triggers in the game it's to be able to preempively ritual-cast a spell that would require a lot of successes (more than you would be able to get on an Arete roll) and you wouldn't want to be &quot;on&quot; all the time because it's inconvinient (again, Iron Avatar it's a good example)\u200b. So casting when the Effect it's triggered would defeat the purpose<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are wards vulgar?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Depends on what the Ward does. If it would be Vulgar then it's Vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T08:48:10-07:00","id":1534947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534942#post1534942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vulgarity, as it pertains to casting difficulty and paradox accrual, is determined by what the consensus thinks of the spell when it is cast. Because Wards don't tend to have visible effects at casting, they are usually coincidental. Reality might object when they start getting active, but that objection will manifest as unbelief rather than paradox points or backlashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this I have to disagree a bit, but not in terms of RAW or anything, but just personal preference. I know that the debate on what exactly counts as an &quot;observer&quot; rages on in the flame wars of the forums webwide, but I stick to the idea of the &quot;Omniscient Observer&quot;. There is, &quot;Reality&quot; (with capital &quot;R&quot;) is not tricked by a sleight of hands; just because human eyes can't see an effect, it doesn't mean that Reality won't.<br /> <br /> So, what that means is, if I enclosure myself in a coffin, then teleport to another enclosured coffin and then teleport back to my original one, outside HUMAN observers wouldn't know any better - but Reality will still abhor my actions with Paradox.<br /> <br /> In the case of a ward, sure thing it is imperceptible to observers - but for Reality, that's still something that shouldn't be there. Of course, if the ward itself is Coincidental (say, a simple &quot;Detect Life&quot; ward) then it is Coincidental, but if the effects of the ward is Vulgar, then it is Vulgar - cave entrances that burn angry people don't just simply occur naturally, therefore Reality abhor the existence of such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T09:53:15-07:00","id":1534949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534947#post1534947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this I have to disagree a bit, but not in terms of RAW or anything, but just personal preference. I know that the debate on what exactly counts as an &quot;observer&quot; rages on in the flame wars of the forums webwide, but I stick to the idea of the &quot;Omniscient Observer&quot;. There is, &quot;Reality&quot; (with capital &quot;R&quot;) is not tricked by a sleight of hands; just because human eyes can't see an effect, it doesn't mean that Reality won't.<br /> <br /> So, what that means is, if I enclosure myself in a coffin, then teleport to another enclosured coffin and then teleport back to my original one, outside HUMAN observers wouldn't know any better - but Reality will still abhor my actions with Paradox.<br /> <br /> In the case of a ward, sure thing it is imperceptible to observers - but for Reality, that's still something that shouldn't be there. Of course, if the ward itself is Coincidental (say, a simple &quot;Detect Life&quot; ward) then it is Coincidental, but if the effects of the ward is Vulgar, then it is Vulgar - cave entrances that burn angry people don't just simply occur naturally, therefore Reality abhor the existence of such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you want to run it you can, but as you say its not the rules. There is already a system for handling spells that aren't obviously impossible but become so over time, and that is unbelief.<br /> <br /> Also, the Hypothetical Omniscient Observer isn't supposed to be omniscient. I know that sounds silly, but the core idea was that under HOO you can't hide an otherwise vulgar effect by doing it where a typical observer can't see (like your coffin example). It wasn't supposed to give the typical observer inhuman powers like looking into the future and seeing what a ward would eventually look like.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, M20 gave an incredibly uncharitable and useless description of the idea and made it look like something that suspended the rules rather than fitting into them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T09:56:30-07:00","id":1534950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534908#post1534908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you share?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. I didn't expand because I thought you were interested in the rules as written, not in house rules. But in the case of wards, they are so vague and poorly written that I do recommend people to hunt for some good house rules instead.<br /> <br /> One thing to note is that my own tables play with heavily modified rules, I have basically re-wrote all of the Spheres because I utterly dislike the utter mess rules they have, but I'll try to stick as close as possible to raw.<br /> <br /> What Ramnesis wrote above is actually pretty close to what I use, which just some minor modifications; for instance, I consider Vulgar Wards (those that &quot;unleash&quot; Vulgar effects when triggered) to be Vulgar, even if nobody is watching (it's the difference between &quot;Vulgar with no witnesses&quot; and &quot;with witnesses&quot;).<br /> <br /> Second, under my house rules, all Triggers require Entropy 2. It actually requires a combination of Entropy 1 + Entropy 2, but because Entropy 2 already obviously contains Entropy 1 already, there's no need to state Entropy 1 also.<br /> <br /> I'll explain: Entropy 1 is needed to &quot;identify the circumstances&quot;, meaning that it is what the Ward uses to &quot;identify&quot; the targets. So, if your ward is supposed to activate exclusively on targets that are angry and wearing a red cloth made of cotton, then it is Entropy 1 that will make that selection and exclude targets that don't fit the parameters.<br /> <br /> Then Entropy 2 is the actual &quot;Trigger&quot;, basically causing the spell to &quot;fail&quot; when the designed circumstances are not the ones specified. Entropy 2 therefore works as a sort of&quot;switch on/off&quot; for your ward.<br /> <br /> According to RAW (rules as written), Triggers require Time 4 and Entropy 2, but I have always disliked that, first for the massive Spheres requirements - you'd need to have Time 4 just for that, which isn't cheap, and while Entropy 2 is a bit easier, that's just the Trigger, you'll still need whatever other Spheres to actually create the effect.<br /> <br /> Also, that never made much sense for me. One of the problems that I have always thought about in this game is that the writers almost never explain WHY or WHAT each Sphere level in a single effect actually does. Their explanation on what Time 4 is actually doing there is pretty vague at best and nonsensical at worst. &quot;Holding the spell in time&quot; doesn't make much sense if you can just simply spend some successes in extending the duration of it.<br /> <br /> In the case of Wards, it is mandatory to have SOME time extended, since I doubt that a single turn ward would serve for anything. Since the main use of them is to protect a Mage's sanctum, most of the time they would probably be made permanent, and since most of the time a Mage's sanctuary will be fine tuned to his own Paradigm, this means that those will be Coincidental anyway.<br /> <br /> Time 4 would only make sense for Triggers if it were combined with Time 2, as in &quot;hold the spell in suspension until X time&quot;, but that's never hinted or explained in the text of the rules.<br /> <br /> Besides, I don't really see this as a spell being &quot;held on hold&quot;, particularly because you are already using Entropy 2 to cause it to &quot;fail&quot; under pre set conditions. So, imo that's just an unnecessary addition. The spell is not &quot;on hold&quot;, but rather is selectively affecting different targets while being &quot;always on&quot;. It's no different from creating an instantaneous fireball that only incinerates pregnant women (wow my own personal mind, what kind of example was that?)<br /> <br /> So, I always like to explain the reasoning behind every choice of Spheres for an effect, forgive me if that sounds a bit prolix. But in my opinion, that's what truly helps others to use the Sphere system, by comprehending how to build up their own effects based on what each level does in detail. I prefer that way rather than just saying &quot;yeah, just use Entropy 2&quot;, because then you wouldn't understand the reason as to why that is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Entropy 2 for Triggers, and I hope my explanation has made a good case as to why.<br /> <br /> Then you just simply add the desired effects. Like Ramnesis said, a &quot;simple&quot; &quot;You Shall Not Pass!&quot; is Correspondence 4. But you could also build an &quot;Invisible Wall&quot; using Forces 3, but in this case, an intruder could actually force his way in using his muscular strength in an opposed roll, because with Forces 3 you would be creating a sort of &quot;Invisible Hand&quot; that pushes intruders out. Correspondence 4 however creates an area of &quot;Infinite Space&quot;, therefore it just can't be forced in.<br /> <br /> Other effects, just add the Spheres as if you were throwing the effect without being a Ward, then add Entropy 2 and the successes required for the amount of time that you wish it to last.<br /> <br /> For example, a Ward against &quot;Bad Thoughts&quot; that causes anyone that enters the area to enter a state of peace of mind, would require Mind 2 (Mind 2 is basically &quot;Empathetic Magic&quot;, or the manipulation of emotions).<br /> <br /> A Ward that burns intruders would require Forces 3, Prime 2 and 1 point of quint; alternatively, you could use Prime 4 so that you don't need to constantly feed it a quint point for every single cat intruder that it burns.<br /> <br /> Ramnesis claimed for example, that to target a Vampire you'd need Life2/Matter2. I disagree in most cases.<br /> <br /> I also don't think you need anything other than Entropy 1 in order to &quot;discriminate targets&quot;. Sure, Entropy 1 can NOT tell you if a coin is made of gold or lead; however, it doesn't need to. You don't need to identify metals for Entropy. Entropy detects &quot;Destiny&quot;, therefore it is able to discriminate basically anything, without telling you what it is.<br /> <br /> Let me try to explain: you'd need Life 1 to determine if an individual is a male or female. Because Life 1 actually allows you to &quot;see&quot; the individuals' morphology, genetics and so on.<br /> <br /> Entropy however, will just state &quot;0% or 100% chance of being female&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can't detect emotions with Entropy 1, for that you need Mind 1, but you CAN use Entropy 1 to determine, in a room full of people, which one is the angriest of the mob.<br /> <br /> So, you don't need anything other than Entropy 1 for the, let's call it, &quot;Lock On Target&quot; effect required for the Ward.<br /> <br /> Thus, you need Entropy 1 for the &quot;Lock on Target&quot; part of the effect;<br /> Entropy 2 for the &quot;Conditional Trigger&quot; part of the effect<br /> And then whatever other Spheres for whatever other effects you wish to integrate.<br /> <br /> But what about targeting Vampires? Sure, you need Life 2 + Matter 2 to affect Vampires... But in my opinion, that is EXCLUSIVELY for effects that specifically target their Pattern. What I mean by this is, if you want to launch a &quot;vampiric flu disease&quot; at them, or if you want to shapeshift them, then you'd need Life2/Matter2 in addition to whatever other effects; but NOT if you want to read their minds or rip off their souls (with Spirit 5).<br /> <br /> What's more, if you're just throwing a fireball, or in the case of a ward, incinerate vampiric intruders, then no, you don't need Life2 Matter2 combo, because the &quot;target&quot; is actually a &quot;fire in the hole&quot; being shot at where they are at. So, a simple Ward of Entropy 2, Forces 3, Prime 2 + 1 quint (or Prime 4 and no quint) would suffice.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Arete roll, number of successes, amount of damage, duration, reach and any other considerations about the magnitude of the Ward, those are all done when the Ward is created. You create the Ward in a ritual and stipulate how many successes you'll need and how many successes you want to expend on duration, damage and so on.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T10:00:11-07:00","id":1534951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534949#post1534949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's how you want to run it you can, but as you say its not the rules. There is already a system for handling spells that aren't obviously impossible but become so over time, and that is unbelief.<br /> <br /> Also, the Hypothetical Omniscient Observer isn't supposed to be omniscient. I know that sounds silly, but the core idea was that under HOO you can't hide an otherwise vulgar effect by doing it where a typical observer can't see (like your coffin example). It wasn't supposed to give the typical observer inhuman powers like looking into the future and seeing what a ward would eventually look like.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, M20 gave an incredibly uncharitable and useless description of the idea and made it look like something that suspended the rules rather than fitting into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm aware that this is my own house rules and not raw. I dislike the raw in this case.<br /> <br /> &quot;Coincidental&quot; in my games most of the times is only sensorial magic and most of Entropy and Mind, and things that COULD (no matter how improbable) happen without being the Mage's doing.<br /> <br /> But again, that's me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T11:32:48-07:00","id":1534956,"title":"","content":"Hmm personally i go by: There is always a Steve watching. Steve is of a typical build and does not have good memmory. If steve fits somewhere then hes watching. So he cant be with you in the coffin but he can go with you to the closet :P<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your answers.<br /> <br /> For triggers i think ill go with the idea that with time 4 you scry the future when the trigger happens and send the spell through time to activate at that moment. Meaning time 4 will be enough to send things forward in time.<br /> <br /> For wards i like the idea that locking detects the specified targets when they enter the area. Its an advanced way of giving the ward the sensory 1 sphere effects. I also think it could be replaced by Entropy 4 as it allows to manipulate destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-30-2024, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T20:42:30-07:00","id":1534979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534956#post1534956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm personally i go by: There is always a Steve watching. Steve is of a typical build and does not have good memmory. If steve fits somewhere then hes watching. So he cant be with you in the coffin but he can go with you to the closet :P<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your answers.<br /> <br /> For triggers i think ill go with the idea that with time 4 you scry the future when the trigger happens and send the spell through time to activate at that moment. Meaning time 4 will be enough to send things forward in time.<br /> <br /> For wards i like the idea that locking detects the specified targets when they enter the area. Its an advanced way of giving the ward the sensory 1 sphere effects. I also think it could be replaced by Entropy 4 as it allows to manipulate destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy 4 isn't manipulating destiny, that would be Entropy 5. Entropy 4 manipulates &quot;randomness&quot; in living Patterns. Entropy 2 should suffice, since it deals with manipulating probabilities, so it causes your spell to &quot;fail&quot; if it does not meet whatever criteria. But, if you think that's &quot;too easy&quot;, then it would have to be full blown Entropy 5.<br /> <br /> But in my opinion, Entropy 5 with deal with more &quot;severe&quot; conditions other than &quot;affect only pregnant women&quot;. A Ward with Entropy 5 would be something more like &quot;at the age of 18, that girl will hit the nail of a...&quot; - sorry, English is not my mother tongue, so I don't know the name of the preindustrial machine that makes cloth... But it's that thing &quot;... And then she will sleep a dreamless and deathless sleep (just don't read the small letters that say that a true love's kiss can remove this state)&quot;<br /> <br /> Time 4... Yes, it could work. But then you would have to use another Time 2 effect to actually look into the future to keep the spell on hold until such a time, otherwise you would just randomly unleash the spell at a future time. Time 4 puts a &quot;hold&quot; on spells, it is Time 2 that &quot;sees&quot; the future. The problem is that the future apparently is not fixed, and even if it is, the ability to spy on it is unreliable at best. But Time alone cannot set conditions for the spell to be triggered, for that you do need Entropy. The only &quot;condition&quot; you can set with time alone is a... Time condition.<br /> <br /> Putting spells on hold using Time 4 is more useful to make a sort of &quot;timed grenade spell&quot;. Sure, you can create a bomb that blows after 1 minute, Forces 3, Prime 2, Time 4, 1 quint. That's the unimaginative common use (besides, there are mundane bombs that do just that). But you could in theory use it for any sort of arcane &quot;timed bombs&quot;. A spell of lust using Mind that &quot;blows&quot; after a minute, so you &quot;drop&quot; the spell in a place, run away and your pursuers will enter the room only to be overwhelmed by a Dionysian fever... Just set the cameras and sell the results on OF...<br /> <br /> Cof cof... Anyway, you get my point.<br /> <br /> However, it's your game. Do as you please. Those are just my 2 cents on the subject<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T02:09:39-07:00","id":1534989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534979#post1534979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entropy 4 isn't manipulating destiny, that would be Entropy 5. Entropy 4 manipulates &quot;randomness&quot; in living Patterns. Entropy 2 should suffice, since it deals with manipulating probabilities, so it causes your spell to &quot;fail&quot; if it does not meet whatever criteria. But, if you think that's &quot;too easy&quot;, then it would have to be full blown Entropy 5.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My entropy sphere looks like this:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Sense probablility<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Manipulate predictable* ongoing probability processes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Create predictable probability processes, manipulate complicated** praobability processes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Create complicated** probability processes, heal, decay<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Shape destiny<br /> * a predictable process is a process where no will is involwed<br /> ** a complicated process is one where will is involved<br /> <br /> As for time 4 and future consistency i play with novicow self consistency principle so time is mostly fixed. You can change wariables but its like tossing a peble into the river. If you have gone back in time means you already did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 05-01-2024, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T06:46:53-07:00","id":1534997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534989#post1534989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My entropy sphere looks like this:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span> Sense probablility<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Manipulate predictable* ongoing probability processes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Create predictable probability processes, manipulate complicated** praobability processes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Create complicated** probability processes, heal, decay<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0</span></span>\u200b Shape destiny<br /> * a predictable process is a process where no will is involwed<br /> ** a complicated process is one where will is involved<br /> <br /> As for time 4 and future consistency i play with novicow self consistency principle so time is mostly fixed. You can change wariables but its like tossing a peble into the river. If you have gone back in time means you already did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also use fixed time; I don't however like to use Time to just simply ruin anything because you always perfectly know everything that'll come to pass ahead. So, despite using fixed time, I don't make seeing into past or future an ability that is crystal clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T06:58:06-07:00","id":1534999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534950#post1534950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, under my house rules, all Triggers require Entropy 2. It actually requires a combination of Entropy 1 + Entropy 2, but because Entropy 2 already obviously contains Entropy 1 already, there's no need to state Entropy 1 also.<br /> <br /> I'll explain: Entropy 1 is needed to &quot;identify the circumstances&quot;, meaning that it is what the Ward uses to &quot;identify&quot; the targets. So, if your ward is supposed to activate exclusively on targets that are angry and wearing a red cloth made of cotton, then it is Entropy 1 that will make that selection and exclude targets that don't fit the parameters.<br /> <br /> Then Entropy 2 is the actual &quot;Trigger&quot;, basically causing the spell to &quot;fail&quot; when the designed circumstances are not the ones specified. Entropy 2 therefore works as a sort of&quot;switch on/off&quot; for your ward.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do things this way too. And you could also use Entropy alone to set the conditions that end the time suspension part of the spell too, releasing the rest of the spell into the world. I'd probably require more successes for using Entropy than for using specific domain spheres. My rationale is that the domain spheres have an easier time detecting their own domain. Entropy can do it, but it is more complicated and hence needs more successes.<br /> <br /> I consider the trigger part of the effect to be included in Time 4. It's in the name of the ability, after all. So if other spheres are used to set the conditions, the mage doesn't also need Entropy to set the trigger. The same goes for Wards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534979#post1534979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But in my opinion, Entropy 5 with deal with more &quot;severe&quot; conditions other than &quot;affect only pregnant women&quot;. A Ward with Entropy 5 would be something more like &quot;at the age of 18, that girl will hit the nail of a...&quot; - sorry, English is not my mother tongue, so I don't know the name of the preindustrial machine that makes cloth... But it's that thing &quot;... And then she will sleep a dreamless and deathless sleep (just don't read the small letters that say that a true love's kiss can remove this state)&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The machine that makes cloth is a loom. The machine from the fairy tale is a spinning wheel, which makes thread. The specific part that she pricked her finger with was a spindle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time 4... Yes, it could work. But then you would have to use another Time 2 effect to actually look into the future to keep the spell on hold until such a time, otherwise you would just randomly unleash the spell at a future time. Time 4 puts a &quot;hold&quot; on spells, it is Time 2 that &quot;sees&quot; the future. The problem is that the future apparently is not fixed, and even if it is, the ability to spy on it is unreliable at best. But Time alone cannot set conditions for the spell to be triggered, for that you do need Entropy. The only &quot;condition&quot; you can set with time alone is a... Time condition. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I wrote up an entire response saying this exact thing until I saw you covered it.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T07:53:21-07:00","id":1535007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1534997#post1534997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also use fixed time; I don't however like to use Time to just simply ruin anything because you always perfectly know everything that'll come to pass ahead. So, despite using fixed time, I don't make seeing into past or future an ability that is crystal clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume its clear for the time 4 trigger effect. You scry to find the nearest instance of X and send the spell there. Therefore i think its not exactly time 2 thats shows you the future but time 4 that sends the spell to a chosen event in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T08:45:22-07:00","id":1535013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535007#post1535007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume its clear for the time 4 trigger effect. You scry to find the nearest instance of X and send the spell there. Therefore i think its not exactly time 2 thats shows you the future but time 4 that sends the spell to a chosen event in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way triggers work is that the spell is cast but suspended outside of time until certain conditions are met. The mage doesn't need to look into the future to cast it. Scrying the future and casting into it is a different effect (and a different rank). <br /> <br /> Also, as a practical matter, casting into the future is always going to be an iffy proposition in a roleplaying game as you never know what the players will do to change things. Even if time is fixed, the ST can't know what it will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T09:25:06-07:00","id":1535016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535013#post1535013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way triggers work is that the spell is cast but suspended outside of time until certain conditions are met. The mage doesn't need to look into the future to cast it. Scrying the future and casting into it is a different effect (and a different rank).<br /> <br /> Also, as a practical matter, casting into the future is always going to be an iffy proposition in a roleplaying game as you never know what the players will do to change things. Even if time is fixed, the ST can't know what it will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you did not understand what i mean. Example:<br /> the caster casts a triggered spell to crate a gravity field with forces around him self so the projectiles that would hit him orbit around him instead. The spell is triggered to a time when someone will fire a projectile at him so he scryes that moment and sends the spell there. He did not see the moment while scrying this way nor will he know when that happens. Only the spell does. The spell is just sent to the right time in the timeline on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 05-01-2024, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T10:00:05-07:00","id":1535022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535016#post1535016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you did not understand what i mean. Example:<br /> the caster casts a triggered spell to crate a gravity field with forces around him self so the projectiles that would hit him orbit around him instead. The spell is triggered to a time when someone will fire a projectile at him so he scryes that moment and sends the spell there. He did not see the moment while scrying this way nor will he know when that happens. Only the spell does. The spell is just sent to the right time in the timeline on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly consistent with how a trigger spell functions, which makes it as good an explanation as any. However, if the mage is not directing the spell himself, it still needs to direct itself to the right conditions. The Time sphere really can't identify the projectile or the zone on its own. I'd still use some kind of sphere combination to set the conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T19:12:28-07:00","id":1535047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535016#post1535016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you did not understand what i mean. Example:<br /> the caster casts a triggered spell to crate a gravity field with forces around him self so the projectiles that would hit him orbit around him instead. The spell is triggered to a time when someone will fire a projectile at him so he scryes that moment and sends the spell there. He did not see the moment while scrying this way nor will he know when that happens. Only the spell does. The spell is just sent to the right time in the timeline on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh.... I see what your reasoning behind it was now.<br /> <br /> But that's not how the Time Sphere works.<br /> <br /> The time Sphere is not &quot;conditional&quot;. What I mean by it is that, you can't set conditions for it, except based on time alone. And by, based on time alone, it means based on some predetermined amount of time at the time of casting. For instance: &quot;stop holding after a month&quot;.<br /> <br /> Conditions can only be set by Entropy, because Entropy is essentially a &quot;conditional Sphere&quot;.<br /> <br /> I get it what you mean, you're saying &quot;hold a spell until such a time upon which a bald man enters this area&quot;, and that Time 4 Sphere would then determine WHEN in the future there will be a bald guy passing, just as if the mage was scrying into the future himself, however the mage is not doing the scrying, the spell is, and then the spell simply says &quot;bald guy, one week from now&quot; and then the spell itself gets set to hold for 1 week. I got what you meant here. But Time Sphere doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> First of all, the problem is that scrying into the future (or past) is not precise; at beast, you could get an estimated time upon which a bald guy will pass (&quot;a bald guy will pass sometime from now up to 1 week). And that lack of precision would cause the spell to automatically fail, because the holding of Time 4 requires a precise time frame.<br /> <br /> Secondly, time holding a spell doesn't allow for the spell to &quot;re-weave&quot; itself after &quot;use&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even if it was possible for the spell to determine with precision the future event that you wish to target, the spell would remain on hold until triggered ONCE. After being unleashed, the spell then would be spent.Gone.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Time 4 alone is a poor fit for a Ward, even if it could be used to predetermine a future event, because it only works once.<br /> <br /> Entropy, however, can make a spell to &quot;selectively fail&quot;, which is why it is the perfect fit for a spell with a &quot;switch&quot; and with predetermined conditions.<br /> <br /> Entropy is also THE conditional Sphere.<br /> <br /> The way I like to build effects in Mage is more or less like building a computer algorithm. Which is why I always return to the descriptions of the levels on each Sphere, and why Im always so adamant about them being well written (spoilers: they are not). And also why I also always go to the table for Duration, Reach and Successes needed for effects when I want to say that some X level on A Sphere is poorly written, because to me, the way it should work should be:<br /> - Desired effect;<br /> - Look at the best Spheres that probably fit;<br /> - Look at the descriptions on each level.<br /> - Try to segment the Effect into sensible parts<br /> <br /> So, Entropy is the default Sphere for &quot;If, Then&quot; conditional effects, which is a common feature for computational algorithms.<br /> <br /> &quot;If a blind child passes, then unleashes X&quot; is the bread and butter of Entropy 2. &quot;If Im allied with Target, then no damage&quot;, is the basic algorithm for Entropy 2, Forces 3, Prime 2 to create &quot;selective fireballs&quot;.<br /> <br /> Rules as written, Triggers require Time 4 AND Entropy 2. The reasoning for Entropy 2 is as I described, but unfortunately the official text is a lot more vague than what I described, not really explaining it too well.<br /> <br /> That's one thing that I really think that is missing in Mage, thorough explanations for the reasoning behind each Spheres selected for any given effect.<br /> <br /> This lack of clarity causes the writers themselves to not know what their doing; that's by the way my own personal reasoning for discarding Time 4 from triggers. It seems that, the writers reasoning behind that choice is for the spell to &quot;Remain on hold&quot; until being triggered by Entropy 2 under the correct set of circumstances; but that to me doesn't seem right, because Entropy 2 alone already causes a spell to &quot;selectively fail&quot; without the need to be put on hold, and Time is a poor fit due to all of the explanations I gave above already - no precise time frame, and Time can only be used ONCE, upon which the spell is spent.<br /> <br /> A conditional spell with a Trigger cannot, therefore, have Time 4 as a prerequisite for the Trigger, because even if Entropy 2 could bypass the &quot;precise time frame&quot; for its activation, Time cannot re-activate a spell spent.<br /> <br /> Entropy on the other hand, doesn't require the spell to be &quot;re-activated&quot; as Time would, because in truth, the spell will ALWAYS remain &quot;always on&quot; all the time, the reason why the effects aren't constantly happening is because Entropy causes the spell to &quot;selectively fail&quot; at most of the time, except under the set conditions, upon which it &quot;doesn't fail anymore&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hence why, for me, all Conditional Triggers are done with Entropy 2 (+ desired effects).<br /> <br /> But I can also see how some other Spheres may be required, like what Ramnesis said, for instance, a &quot;Ward against Rats&quot; may require Life 1 to &quot;detect rats&quot; plus Forces 3/Prime 4 to electrocute them (without needing quint points to fuel), although in my opinion, Entropy 1 (already contained in Entropy 2) can already do that without needing to add Life 1, but not because Entropy 1 is capable to discern the living Patterns of rats, but rather because Entropy 1 will simply &quot;say to your spell&quot; &quot;I feel a disturbance in the Force. I think it is about time to stop selectively failing and to succeed in electrocuting something&quot;. Thus, Entropy 1 can dictate whatever target you desire, be it a Spirit, a mental construct floating in the Ether, an ethereal emanation of resonance, a rat or a piece of gold. Entropy 1 won't tell you what the Pattern is, but it will tell you &quot;the probabilities have matched. Time to act&quot;, and Entropy 2 will &quot;Switch On&quot; the spell based on that.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T19:27:29-07:00","id":1535048,"title":"","content":"Entropy 1 is basically the &quot;Ubermensch&quot; of the Level 1 Spheres, and the reason is because it can indirectly detect almost anything, but even if its indirect, it is no less precise.<br /> <br /> Think of it as if we were nuclear physicists detecting particles. We have a machine that tells us when a particle passes by; we have no idea what particles are passing, we don't know if they are neutrinos or quarks or whatever, but WE KNOW WHEN A PARTICLE PASSES.<br /> <br /> That's more or less how Entropy 1 works. Yes, you can identify if there are rats under the attic of your house. You won't get Skyrim green lights above your head as if it were Life 1, but you'll see them nevertheless as &quot;quantum probabilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can use Entropy 1 to spot a guy with a gun in the middle of a crowd, even thou you don't have Matter 1.<br /> <br /> And that's because you go by &quot;probabilities&quot; or &quot;destiny&quot; alone.<br /> <br /> That's why, Entropy 1 is the ultimate &quot;Detector of Conditions&quot;.<br /> <br /> And finally, Entropy 2 is the simple &quot;Switch&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's what Triggers are, when we are building this Algorithm; Triggers require A) A Detector to detect the set conditions and B) A Switch.<br /> <br /> Hence, Entropy 1+ Entropy 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T01:30:08-07:00","id":1535055,"title":"","content":"The problem with this reasoning is time already has a had time to be apealing and Triggered spells is the best thing it has.<br /> <br /> We could asume that time 4 is the sphere of sending things into the future, Knowing when anything will happen (remember spheres clash a lot example entropy 4 healing) and time stoping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T13:51:37-07:00","id":1535086,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a>, I agree with Entropy 2 as an universal trigger, but I don't think it would be the most effective trigger. I would want at least a couple extra successes for an Entropy trigger when a specialized Sphere could apply, like Life.<br /> <br /> Specialized Spheres would suffice at 1 as a trigger, too.<br /> <br /> Time definitely can and does &quot;restart&quot; the spell. As an example, a Time triggered spell could trigger once a week, or any other reccuring time frame.<br /> <br /> Now, seriously, I think you would like Mage the Awakening rules far more than Ascension, and you can adapt them for the setting no problem. I really think it's worth a try.<br /> <br /> On using Time 4 as a universal trigger, I don't see a problem. It's a weird reasoning, but then it is also a Sphere at 4, and Time nonetheless, a particularly hard Sphere to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T03:22:38-07:00","id":1535098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535086#post1535086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a>, I agree with Entropy 2 as an universal trigger, but I don't think it would be the most effective trigger. I would want at least a couple extra successes for an Entropy trigger when a specialized Sphere could apply, like Life.<br /> <br /> Specialized Spheres would suffice at 1 as a trigger, too.<br /> <br /> Time definitely can and does &quot;restart&quot; the spell. As an example, a Time triggered spell could trigger once a week, or any other reccuring time frame.<br /> <br /> Now, seriously, I think you would like Mage the Awakening rules far more than Ascension, and you can adapt them for the setting no problem. I really think it's worth a try.<br /> <br /> On using Time 4 as a universal trigger, I don't see a problem. It's a weird reasoning, but then it is also a Sphere at 4, and Time nonetheless, a particularly hard Sphere to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is i dont realy like awakening. From Nwod i think vampire, mummy and changeling are superior but the rest not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T04:29:13-07:00","id":1535099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534903-wards-and-trigger-spells?p=1535055#post1535055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this reasoning is time already has a had time to be apealing and Triggered spells is the best thing it has.<br /> <br /> We could asume that time 4 is the sphere of sending things into the future, Knowing when anything will happen (remember spheres clash a lot example entropy 4 healing) and time stoping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Definitely, Time's most OP capability is the ability to pierce into the past and future. Time 2 is an absolute overkill. But then again, I'm a huge fan of sensorial magic above all else, a lot more than the most flamboyant effects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}